			  "Agents": {
			    "Internal": {
			      "Version": "1.1.0"
			    }
			  },
			  "CustomInstructions": "This model covers hourly electricity data for Italy, France, Germany and the Netherlands from January 2024, sourced from ENTSO-E.\n- All times are UTC.\n- \"Clean\", \"green\" or \"low emissions\" means low Carbon Intensity gCO2e/kWh. \"Greenest hour\" means the hour with the lowest carbon intensity.\n- Always use the measures for ratios (Renewable %, Low-carbon %, Carbon Intensity); never average stored percentage columns.\n- When reporting carbon intensity, also mention Factor Coverage %. If coverage is below 90%, say the figure is less reliable.\n- Netherlands renewables are under-reported by ENTSO-E (rooftop solar is missing, a large share is classified as \"Other\"); mention this when answering about the Netherlands.\n- Renewable targets are official 2030 national targets, not current-year targets.\n- Prices are day-ahead wholesale prices in EUR/MWh, not consumer prices.\n- If a question is outside this data (other countries, consumer bills, forecasts), say so instead of guessing.\n- Never derive a share by subtracting other shares from 100%. Storage and Other (unclassified) exist, so the remaining share is not fossil, clean or any single group. Always compute a share directly with a filter or an existing measure."
			}
		contentType: json

